# .wolf/memory.md is an append-at-tail session log written by several concurrent
# Claude/Codex sessions, so every branch appends rows at the same place and every
# PR conflicts there. `merge=union` is git's built-in driver: it keeps both sides'
# lines instead of raising a conflict. Ordering within a merge is not guaranteed,
# which is fine for a log read by timestamp. Only this file — buglog.json (JSON)
# and cerebrum.md (edited in place, by section) must still conflict loudly.
.wolf/memory.md merge=union
